Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 54/90] Faster loads with big mod packs: shapes deduplicated by
 hash, data folders read by several threads

Behaviours::build looked each state's collision shape up among the shapes so far by a linear search: quadratic, minutes with a modded pack's 200k states (two threads at 100% through a warm start). It is a hash map by the shape's identity now (VoxelShape::identity_key). json_folder::read opened and read a folder's files one at a time; with tens of thousands (a pack's recipes, loot tables, item models) that took minutes on every start; read_all uses several threads for folders over 512 files, in the same order.

UMP, 184 mods, warm start on an SSD: items 111 -> 46 s, item models 112 -> 37 s, network recipes 94 -> 36 s, recipes 75 -> 32 s; ready 1090 -> 896 s.
